          "date": "2026-05-20 22:30:12.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-19921 ptlrpc: atomic switch in nodemap_export_refresh",
        "message": "LU-19921 ptlrpc: atomic switch in nodemap_export_refresh\n\nThe nodemap_export_refresh() temporarily leaves the export\nwith a NULL ted_nodemap because it calls nodemap_del_member()\nfollowed by nm_member_add(). This creates a window where the\nexport is live but has no nodemap assigned, which violates\nthe invariant that a live export must always have a valid\nted_nodemap and can cause panic.\n\nRefactor the code by extracting the atomic switch logic from\nnm_member_reclassify_nodemap() into a new shared helper function,\nnm_member_reclassify_export(). Update nodemap_export_refresh()\nand nm_member_reclassify_nodemap() to use this helper, ensuring\nthat the ted_nodemap pointer is always updated atomically under\nthe appropriate locks.\n\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-sec\nSigned-off-by: Di Wang <ddiwang@google.com>\nChange-Id: Id1b9fbef61bd5d5d284924f43ef9952378304540\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
